From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Jun 2026 04:09:14 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02251/11362] [outer-loop] E3 into agent: pure-model planner
 (plan_in_model) + harness-friendly wiring

The missing validated piece was plan-in-model -> execute (plan_and_execute ran its OWN
env, wrong for a harness-driven agent). New plan_in_model(engine, is_done, start_grid):
BFS a win path ENTIRELY inside the induced engine (zero real actions), with _model_
candidates (keyboard + salience-ordered object clicks on the predicted grid). E3AgentPolicy
now: explore->collect transitions->induce(proposer)->VERIFY->plan_in_model from the reset
grid->execute step-wise, halting on divergence. Efficiency win = few REAL actions vs the
explorer's 10k+. Validation scripts/arc_e3_agent_solve.py runs the full pipeline on one
game (codex dev proposer; --local for the offline GGUF), collecting transitions INCLUDING
a banked win so is_level_complete is grounded. cd82 codex run in flight.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
